  "title": "The Bike Helmet Is Not a Costume",
  "family": "learning",
  "category": "public safety/preparedness",
  "premise": "A young character wants to use a helmet in a safety poster, but the illustration treats any headwear as equivalent. A reviewed version depicts an appropriate certified helmet and refers fit decisions to current official and manufacturer guidance.",
  "hook": "What makes this safety gear more than a hat?",
  "visible_action": "A costume hat silhouette separates from a helmet icon; certification, condition, and fit-review cards appear without adjustment instructions.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Protective equipment has intended uses and guidance that a decorative look cannot replace.",
  "gate": "Require authoritative bicycle-helmet guidance; avoid unverified fitting steps, impact tests, or guarantees against injury. Do not ask viewers to guess an emergency response or choose an action in a simulated emergency; any response content must come from reviewed official guidance.",
